# Regression fixture for inc-fiiq: overlapping magic circles must not stack.
#
# The character is Neutral EVIL on purpose.  A torch archon's circle inflicts
# its -3 penalty on MA_EVIL creatures only (lib/wspells.irh:3847-3849), so an
# evil player standing between two archons is the only oracle in the game that
# shows the summed value on screen: the "Hit:" line of the side panel.
#
# Three dumps: no circle, one circle, two circles.  The ruling is that the
# second circle adds nothing, so dump two must equal dump one.

a       # Create a New Character
n       # Do not alter the chargen options
y       # Accept Explore Mode
i       # Race: Orc
a       # Subrace: Orc (Standard)
a       # Class: Barbarian
a       # Attributes: first offered set
e       # Alignment: Neutral EVIL -- the whole point of this fixture
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y
y
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

w
y
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@dump:hit-base

# The player stands at the centre.  Radius is 2, so an archon one square away
# and an archon two squares away both cover the player.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "torch archon"
RIGHT ENTER
@dump:hit-one

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Celestials"
@choose "torch archon"
RIGHT RIGHT ENTER
@dump:hit-two

# Both rows must still exist -- the fix suppresses one at read time, it does
# not delete it.  Deleting it would break the leave path this bead is about.
w
@choose "Examine Player Data"
DOWN*40
@dump:player-stati
ESC
ESC
a
